course: dictionary
lesson: 8961
title: Simplify: making things clearer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To simplify something is to make it simpler or easier to understand or do. You take away the extra bits so the main idea is clear.
explain: In maths, to simplify a fraction, you divide the top and bottom by the same number. «Simplify 6/8» means write it as 3/4, which is the same amount with smaller numbers.
explain: Writers and game makers simplify too. «Every game must simplify» the real world, so a game may leave out things like tiredness or cold. Ask yourself: what has been left out, and why?
fact: Simplify is a verb: simplify, simplifies, simplified, simplifying.
fact: «Simplify 2a + 3a» means 5a, because you collect the like terms together.
fact: A fraction is in its simplest form when the top and bottom cannot both be divided by the same number again.
fact: «History games simplify the past», so check what they show against books and people who know the history.
fact: «"I know that I know nothing" is a simplified version of what Plato wrote.» A simplified version is shorter and clearer, with some detail left out.
exercise: «Simplify 6/8.» What is the simplest form? | *3/4 | 6/8 | 2/8
exercise: «Simplify 2a + 3a.» What does it become? | 23a | 6a | *5a
exercise: «Games can teach geography, but they simplify.» What does simplify mean here? | Make it longer and full of detail | Stop it from being played | *Leave out details to make it clearer | Prove that it is true
test: «Simplify 4/10.» What is the simplest form? | 4/10 | 1/10 | 4/5 | *2/5
test: «Simplify 3a + 4a.» What does it become? | 3a4a | 34a | 12a | *7a
exam: «"I know that I know nothing" is a simplified version of what Plato wrote.» What does simplified version mean? | A longer version with extra detail added | A version of the same words written in a different order | *A shorter, clearer version with some detail left out | A version written in another language
